cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Observability Boundaries for Near-Critical Weil Blocks: A Finite-Dimensional Analysis of Off-Line Zero Collisions"
type: article
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-21
authors:
  - family-names: Wakita
    given-names: Yasuyuki
    alias: Mechanic-Y
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mechanic-Y/Observability-Boundaries-Weil-Blocks"
url: "https://mechanic-y.github.io/Observability-Boundaries-Weil-Blocks/"
abstract: >-
  A fixed finite-dimensional single-pair local analysis of near-critical
  off-line zero collisions in a zero-side matrix of Weil type, including
  an explicit quadratic collision coefficient, exact negative detection
  with vanishing geometric margin, and a higher-order real-symmetric
  transverse-jet classification. The work does not prove the Riemann
  Hypothesis and does not claim a general aggregate or infinite-dimensional result.
keywords:
  - Riemann zeta function
  - Weil explicit formula
  - finite-dimensional spectral analysis
  - matrix perturbation
  - observability
  - transverse jets
